{"availability":"available","full":"agoldst/dfr-browser","name":"dfr-browser","description":"Take a MALLET to disciplinary history","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":99,"forks":37,"created":"2013-09-22T22:33:58Z","updated":"2022-07-11T14:08:08Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"http://agoldst.github.io/dfr-browser/demo","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T05:00:56.484Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T05:00:56.484Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T05:00:56.484Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T14:33:09.392Z","stars":99,"forks":37},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:12:12.642Z","stars":99,"forks":37},{"at":"2026-10-06T17:12:01.256Z","stars":99,"forks":37},{"at":"2026-10-08T21:26:48.783Z","stars":99,"forks":37},{"at":"2026-10-11T11:05:05.984Z","stars":99,"forks":37},{"at":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.694Z","stars":99,"forks":37},{"at":"2026-10-18T05:00:56.484Z","stars":99,"forks":37}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["These files use d3 to provide a way to browse some of a topic model of texts in a web browser, relying entirely on static html and javascript files. For more information, see the main project page at agoldst.github.io/dfr-browser and the working demo, a browser for a 64-topic model of the journal PMLA.","This software is free to use, copy, modify, and distribute under the MIT license (which is to say, please credit me if you do use it). This project skews to my needs as a literary scholar and to my amateurishness as a programmer. No aspect of this code has been systematically tested. Sorry.","I worked on this project in 2013–2019, so some parts of it are behind the times. I developed this specifically to explore models of texts from JSTOR's Data for Research service, which has been replaced by the Constellate \"platform\" for similar but differently-formatted data. This model-browser can be, and has been, adapted for topic models of other corpora. The information needed for adapting it can be found below: details may be fiddly but are not particularly complex (or at least they didn't seem so when I was actively working on this!)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/agoldst/dfr-browser/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"3c5cd18901527bb341262ecbba4fffbd919eb8ca2ffd86d37aed9d20727198d8","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:26:41.583Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.840Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2022-07-11T14:08:08Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.848Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"These files use d3 to provide a way to browse some of a topic model of texts in a web browser, relying entirely on static html and javascript files. For more information, see the main project page at agoldst.github.io/dfr-browser and the working demo, a browser for a 64-topic model of the journal PMLA.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/agoldst/dfr-browser/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"3c5cd18901527bb341262ecbba4fffbd919eb8ca2ffd86d37aed9d20727198d8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/agoldst/dfr-browser/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.840Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/agoldst/dfr-browser/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:51.842Z","hash":"3c5cd18901527bb341262ecbba4fffbd919eb8ca2ffd86d37aed9d20727198d8","originalBytes":31665,"storedBytes":31665,"truncated":false},"enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:14.935Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v0.8.1 alpha","tag":"v0.8.1-alpha","publishedAt":"2019-08-09T16:21:05Z","url":"https://github.com/agoldst/dfr-browser/releases/tag/v0.8.1-alpha"},"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:14.935Z","screenshots":[{"src":"previews/4f967d3fd5c13cb5db30ee32.jpg","kind":"demo","capturedAt":"2026-10-12T08:14:12.122Z","url":"http://agoldst.github.io/dfr-browser/demo"}],"qualityPriority":false,"previewAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T08:14:12.122Z","demoHealth":{"url":"